// rows - never a loop on the processor over the clouds in view (it was gskVisit and the casters' search, every cloud of every view every
// frame, then every cloud's rows written again into the frame's buffers). The processor owns the rows (CLD - 08-scene.js) and sends only
// what changed: a cloud born, its lobes a new run, its recipe made or let go, its size, the sliders its recipe was made with.
//   once a frame  STEP: every cloud's FORMING (its growth eased toward the weather's), its lobes PLACED (their morphs eased, the wind's
//                 shape, its growth from its base up - 06-lobes-billows-puffs.js), its BOX and its body's height for its width
//   each view     VIEW: each cloud placed in the view (the world wraps about the deck's middle), CULLED against the view's camera, its
//                   detail (drawn as its lobes, its puffs left out - 13-gpu-sky.js detail by size), its LIGHT's direction and its glow
//                   against the sun (07-light-shadow.js), its lightning, its counts
//                 NEAR: the clouds within half a screen that can cast (in their order), the clouds wanting a recipe, the clouds waiting for one
//                 CASTERS: each cloud on the screen its casters (the clouds whose shadow falls on it - 17-frame.js's rule), kept a few frames
//                 SCAN: every cloud on the screen its room in the frame's buffers, deck after deck (one workgroup, in the clouds' order)
//                 LAYOUT: its row of the frame's table (its lobes, their extras, its casters' lobes) - its palette, its runs, its records'
//                   tiles, its numbers for the processor's readers
