/* ---- THE SEA KIT IN THE PREFAB EDITOR (user Nov 8 23:14, his sheet gen/sea_src/ref-sea-rocks-corals-nov8.png: "Here are some sprites for you to add on the
   Prefab Editor rocks and corals (that should be breakable)"). Each of its 24 pieces - ROCK 1-8, CORAL 1-4, SEA FAN 1-4, TUBE SPONGE 1-4, SPONGE 1-4, and the second sheet's
   12 (assets16/sea_kit.png / .json, gen/sea_kit.py) - is a PUFF component drawn from its sprite (puffC.art: its index - puffPicJob paints the sprite into the
   puff's frame instead of its painted light; its mask, the sprite's shape on the frame, gives its shape where the sheet isn't loaded and to the Component
   Editor), the rocks ROCK components (a BOULDER: still in the current), and a starter prefab of each (ROCK 1, CORAL 1 ...) - its one part standing on its
   ground line, its size as drawn on the sheet. Like any prefab they go on any deck (an UNDERWATER or CAVE deck's DECK 1: collision - uwHardTop), are
   edited, copied and saved in the Prefab and Component Editors, and blown apart as every DECK 1 plant is (plantsBlast - under the water too, underwaterBlast).
   Put in once each where this browser hasn't got them (never over one of its own, nor one it deleted - hidden) ---- */
