/* ================================================================
   THE GROUND'S SPRITES (engine part 2, Nov 10): the ground's pictures - the far strips behind the land (drawLandBg0), the tree row on the
   meadow's back (drawLandRow), the field's boulders (drawFieldBoulders) - drawn from the art atlas (04-zz-art-atlas.js) by a pass of their
   own into the layer C draws into, after what C drew so far (no GL front). Each picture is in the atlas once, its own pixels; what the old
   code made copies for is done here as it draws:
     - the hour's light and a deck's haze: colour x mul + add (glTint's rule);
     - a biome's repaint of the forest's strips (MOUNTAIN, ICE, SWAMP, VOLCANIC - was bgBioVar's canvases): a pixel's colour from its
       brightness, its rows under its column's top (the picture's column-top table, made once - GS.tops) and its neighbours above / below;
     - the tree row's lean with the wind (a shear about the sprite's foot - gsShear), a falling stalactite's turn and its flips: a matrix of
       the sprite's own before the context's (gsXf);
     - a stalactite's cave colours (was stalPic's hue-shifted canvases): a pixel's brightness in its biome's cave hue (gsHue);
     - a strip sinking out of sight: only the source rows that show (the caller's rectangles);
     - solid quads in the same draw, in order: the strips' skirts down to the water, the row's shade under it.
   Queue a frame's sprites, then gsFlush() draws them in the order queued, inside the context's clip (its stencil's bit 0x80) and scissor
   (ggPassDraw) and the queue's own columns (gsClipX), through the context's own matrix (C.s.m - as drawImage drew):
     gsPic(pic)                                       the picture's facts (made once: its size, column tops, coverage, its foot's colour)
     gsTint(mul, add, a)                              the tint for the sprites queued next (0-1 each; a: alpha)
     gsSprite(F, sx, sy, sw, sh, X0, Y0, X1, Y1, fl, M)   a picture's rectangle onto the screen's (through M, a 6-number matrix, if given);
                                                      false while it isn't in the atlas yet
     gsShear(sw, foot) / gsXf(a, b, c, d, e, f)       such a matrix: a lean about the foot's line / any (one reused array - pass it at once)
     gsHue(h)                                         the cave hue for the sprites queued next (null: none)
     gsSolid(X0, Y0, X1, Y1, col, fl, botL)           a rectangle of colour col (0-255) through the tint (a biome's: its rule at brightness botL)
     gsClipX(R)                                       the next flush shown only over the columns R = [x0, x1, ...] (the context's units,
                                                      a pixel in when its middle is: x0 <= x < x1) - the far strips' lands; null all
     gsFlush()                                        the queue drawn
   fl: GS_NEAR (the nearest pixel - also whenever the context's smoothing is off; a sheet's sprites always), GS_HUE (the cave hue), gsBio(letter, tree) (a biome's repaint). Every GPU call through src/gpu/. The queue is
   one typed array, grown in steps, never shrunk.
   ================================================================ */
const GS_REC = 36, GS_MAX = 65536;                             // (floats a sprite; sprites in one draw at most - more go in the next)
